\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Forward KL vs.\ Reverse KL divergence for fitting a student distribution $P_S$ to a bimodal teacher $P_T$. (a)\nobreakspace  {}The teacher distribution with two modes. (b)\nobreakspace  {}Forward KL is mean-seeking: the student covers both modes but places mass in the inter-mode ``hallucination zone.'' (c)\nobreakspace  {}Reverse KL is mode-seeking: the student concentrates on a single peak, dropping the other mode entirely. Adaptive methods (ToDi, Entropy-Aware OPD) dynamically switch between the two based on teacher confidence.}}{7}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:forward_vs_reverse_kl}{{1}{7}{Forward KL vs.\ Reverse KL divergence for fitting a student distribution $P_S$ to a bimodal teacher $P_T$. (a)~The teacher distribution with two modes. (b)~Forward KL is mean-seeking: the student covers both modes but places mass in the inter-mode ``hallucination zone.'' (c)~Reverse KL is mode-seeking: the student concentrates on a single peak, dropping the other mode entirely. Adaptive methods (ToDi, Entropy-Aware OPD) dynamically switch between the two based on teacher confidence}{figure.1}{}}
